 ### Neural Direct Volume Rendering
-A novel multiscale rendering architecture inspired by UNet and VNet, featuring a multiscale volumetric encoding part and a multiscale 2D decoder connected by DeepDVR modules replacing skip connections [S3, unofficial]. An encoder-decoder architecture inspired by VNet and U-Net, using a DVRUnit in skip connections to project from 3D to 2D feature space, combining lower-resolution multichannel images in U-Net decoder blocks [S3, unofficial]. Connect the volumetric multiscale encoder part of a VNet with the upsampling decoder part of a U-Net by inserting a DVRUnit into the skip connections [S3, unofficial]. Each level performs a volume raymarching network similar to VNetL16-17, rendering a potentially spatially downsampled volume in a latent color space at a reduced image resolution [S3, unofficial]. Combine the lower-resolution multichannel images in the U-Net decoder blocks to produce the final 2D image at the desired resolution [S3, unofficial]. Unlike RenderNet, DVRNet extracts features in object space (independent of camera parameters), uses explicit occlusion modeling via absorption/alpha blending, and avoids excessive downsampling via skip connections [S3, unofficial].
+- **Definition**: A novel multiscale rendering architecture inspired by UNet and VNet, featuring a multiscale volumetric encoding part and a multiscale 2D decoder connected by DeepDVR modules replacing skip connections [S3, unofficial]. It uses a DVRUnit in skip connections to project from 3D to 2D feature space, combining lower-resolution multichannel images in U-Net decoder blocks [S3, unofficial].
+- **Steps**: Connect the volumetric multiscale encoder part of a VNet with the upsampling decoder part of a U-Net by inserting a DVRUnit into the skip connections [S3, unofficial]. Each level performs a volume raymarching network similar to VNetL16-17, rendering a potentially spatially downsampled volume in a latent color space at a reduced image resolution [S3, unofficial]. Combine the lower-resolution multichannel images in the U-Net decoder blocks to produce the final 2D image at the desired resolution [S3, unofficial].
+- **Comparison**: Unlike RenderNet, DVRNet extracts features in object space (independent of camera parameters), uses explicit occlusion modeling via absorption/alpha blending, and avoids excessive downsampling via skip connections [S3, unofficial].
 
 ### Neuralangelo
-A framework for high-fidelity 3D surface reconstruction from RGB images using neural volume rendering, combining multi-resolution 3D hash grids with neural surface rendering without auxiliary data [S4]. Uses numerical gradients to compute higher-order derivatives (e.g., surface normals) as a smoothing operation to stabilize optimization [S4]. Uses coarse-to-fine optimization on hash grids controlling different levels of details [S4]. Samples 3D locations along camera view directions [S4]. Encodes the sampled positions using a multi-resolution hash encoding [S4]. Feeds encoded features into an SDF MLP and a color MLP [S4]. Composites images using SDF-based volume rendering [S4]. Unlike concurrent work [43] which uses a displacement network to correct shape, Neuralangelo uses hierarchical hash grids and controls detail levels based on analysis of higher-order derivatives [S4].
+- **Definition**: A framework for high-fidelity 3D surface reconstruction from RGB images using neural volume rendering, combining multi-resolution 3D hash grids with neural surface rendering without auxiliary data [S4]. It uses numerical gradients to compute higher-order derivatives (e.g., surface normals) as a smoothing operation to stabilize optimization [S4]. It uses coarse-to-fine optimization on hash grids controlling different levels of details [S4].
+- **Steps**: Samples 3D locations along camera view directions [S4]. Encodes the sampled positions using a multi-resolution hash encoding [S4]. Feeds encoded features into an SDF MLP and a color MLP [S4]. Composites images using SDF-based volume rendering [S4].
+- **Comparison**: Unlike concurrent work [43] which uses a displacement network to correct shape, Neuralangelo uses hierarchical hash grids and controls detail levels based on analysis of higher-order derivatives [S4].
 
